{
  "answer": "**答案：Lavodayapura（ละโวทยปุระ，意思是“Lava 起源之城”）。** 英文维基百科《History of Lopburi》写道：“In the 10th century, when it was known as Lavodayapura (Khmer language), Lavo was subordinate to the Khmer empire.”\n\n另外两处来源：\n- 暹罗学会（Siam Society）期刊里 Griswold 和 Prasert 的论文说，吴哥圣剑寺（Prah Khan of Angkor）的碑铭称这座城为 Lavodayapura。\n- 法文的博士论文（Roche 2023）里，这座城也写作 Lavodaya。\n\n依据网址：\n- https://browse.library.kiwix.org/content/wikipedia_en_all_maxi/A/History_of_Lopburi\n- https://kids.kiddle.co/History_of_Lopburi\n- https://thesiamsociety.org/wp-content/uploads/1972/03/JSS_060_1c_GriswoldPrasert_KingLodaiyaOfSukhodayaAndContemporaries.pdf\n\n用了 3 次搜索。",
